{"name":"Equanimity","hex":"#83a9b3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"equanimity","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being calm, stable and composed, especially under stress."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equanimity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Equanimity","blocks":[{"text":"Equanimity is a state of psychological stability and composure which is undisturbed by the experience of or exposure to emotions, pain, or other phenomena that may otherwise cause a loss of mental balance. The virtue and value of equanimity is extolled and advocated by a number of major religions and ancient philosophies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Winslow_Homer_-_The_Gulf_Stream_-_Metropolitan_Museum_of_Art.jpg/330px-Winslow_Homer_-_The_Gulf_Stream_-_Metropolitan_Museum_of_Art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equanimity"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"equanimity":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/08/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-equanimity.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/08/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-equanimity.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-equanimity.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/08/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-equanimity.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-equanimity.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey Bushchat in Sillery Gaon March 2025 by Tisha Mukherjee 01","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_March_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_01.jpg/500px-Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_March_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_01.jpg","ratio":1.3997488488907492,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_